---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, MCP_URL, dlUrl } from '../lib/site.mjs';
import { assets } from '../lib/assets.mjs';
const a = assets[0];
const desktop = JSON.stringify({ mcpServers: { cozu: { type: 'http', url: MCP_URL } } }, null, 2);
const jsonld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle', name: 'Cozu API and MCP server', url: `${SITE}/developers`, about: 'Search and download free 3D models from an agent or a script' }];
const tools = [
  ['search_assets', 'query, category, format, limit', 'Finds models by words, category (vehicles, props...) and format (GLB, OBJ). Returns each match with its page, licence, credit line and main downloads.'],
  ['get_asset', 'id', 'The full record of one model: every file with its URL, size and SHA-256, the stats, previews and the credit line.'],
  ['get_attribution', 'id, format', 'The credit line to add to your project, as text, HTML or Markdown.'],
  ['list_categories', '', 'The categories with how many models each holds.'],
];
const rest = [
  ['GET', '/api/v1/assets.json', 'The whole catalog: every model as a full record.'],
  ['GET', `/api/v1/assets/{id}.json`, `One model, for example /api/v1/assets/${a.slug}.json.`],
  ['GET', '/api/v1/search?q=truck&category=vehicles&format=GLB&limit=10', 'Search, the same as the MCP tool.'],
  ['GET', '/api/v1/openapi.json', 'The OpenAPI 3.1 description of these endpoints.'],
  ['GET', `/assets/{id}.md`, 'A model\'s page as Markdown.'],
  ['GET', '/llms.txt', 'A short index for language models; /llms-full.txt holds every record.'],
];
---
<Base title="API and MCP server for free 3D models | Cozu" description="Search and download Cozu's free 3D models from agents and scripts: an MCP server at cozu.xyz/mcp and a JSON API, with no key and no account." jsonld={jsonld}>
  <section class="section section--page" aria-labelledby="dev-h">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="span-5 page-head">
        <h1 id="dev-h">The API and MCP server</h1>
        <p class="t-lead">Agents and scripts can search the models, download their files and get the credit line. No key, no account, no rate card.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="span-7 prose">
        <h2 id="mcp">Connect an agent</h2>
        <p>The MCP server speaks Streamable HTTP at <code>{MCP_URL}</code>. In Claude Code:</p>
        <pre>claude mcp add --transport http cozu {MCP_URL}</pre>
        <p>In clients configured with JSON (Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code and others):</p>
        <pre>{desktop}</pre>
        <h2 id="skill">Install the skill</h2>
        <p>The Cozu skill tells coding agents when a Cozu model fits, which file to use for each engine, and how to credit it. It works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and other agents, with or without the MCP server:</p>
        <pre>npx skills add y0av/cozu</pre>
        <h2 id="tools">Tools</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Arguments</th><th>What it returns</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{tools.map(([n, args, d]) => <tr><td><code>{n}</code></td><td>{args || 'none'}</td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
        <p>An agent that adds a model to a project should also add its credit line to the project's credits, for example a CREDITS.md file. <code>get_attribution</code> returns it ready to paste.</p>
        <h2 id="rest">JSON API</h2>
        <p>Plain HTTPS with open CORS, so it works from a browser too. Base URL <code>{SITE}</code>.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{rest.map(([m, p, d]) => <tr><td><code>{m} {p}</code></td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
        <pre>curl -s {SITE}/api/v1/assets/{a.slug}.json</pre>
        <h2 id="files">Downloading files</h2>
        <p>File URLs in a record point at <code>{SITE}/dl/</code>, which redirects to the file in Cozu's storage, so follow redirects (<code>curl -L</code>). No sign-in. Each file lists its size in bytes and its SHA-256, so a script can check what it got. A model's files never change under the same version number; a fix ships as a new version with its own URLs.</p>
        <pre>curl -L -O {dlUrl(a, (a.downloads.find((d) => d.file.endsWith('.glb')) ?? a.downloads[0]).file)}</pre>
        <h2 id="limits">Fair use</h2>
        <p>There is no key and no hard limit. Cache the catalog rather than fetching it on every request, and download a package once rather than per build.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
